1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,710
Every perps competition puts you on a leaderboard.

2
00:00:03,660 --> 00:00:06,695
You never beat anyone in particular.

3
00:00:06,695 --> 00:00:08,647
This is a duel.

4
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:15,166
dreamDEX's own arena review: thirty-five percent of trades that went
green still closed red.

5
00:00:15,115 --> 00:00:17,731
A leaderboard cannot fix that.

6
00:00:17,731 --> 00:00:20,792
A PnL screenshot proves nothing.

7
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:25,214
Pick a market, a side, a size, a clock.

8
00:00:25,164 --> 00:00:28,429
No wallet, no faucet, no signup.

9
00:00:28,429 --> 00:00:32,421
The fighter who accepts takes the other side of a real trade.

10
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:36,759
The challenge link is the whole funnel.

11
00:00:36,709 --> 00:00:41,250
A rival opens it, types a name, and accepts the opposite side.

12
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:44,299
Nothing to install, nothing to fund.

13
00:00:44,930 --> 00:00:47,163
Then the fight is real.

14
00:00:47,113 --> 00:00:50,850
Both orders hit the dreamDEX book in parallel.

15
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:55,875
The race is return on margin actually locked, with entry lines on a
live tape.

16
00:00:55,875 --> 00:01:00,595
Either fighter can cash out, and that closes both positions at market.

17
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:04,644
Settlement is a statement, not a screenshot.

18
00:01:04,594 --> 00:01:10,411
Entry, exit, funding, margin locked, net return, all from actual
fills.

19
00:01:10,411 --> 00:01:15,423
Four transaction hashes, one per order, each openable on the explorer.

20
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:18,314
Do not trust the page.

21
00:01:18,264 --> 00:01:25,253
Ask the chain: two opens, two closes, each a confirmed receipt on
Somnia Tokyo, with its own block number.

22
00:01:25,859 --> 00:01:27,825
Then run it back.

23
00:01:27,775 --> 00:01:31,487
Rematch swaps sides and reserves the rival's seat.

24
00:01:31,487 --> 00:01:37,902
The series keeps score, and every fighter carries a record: wins,
losses, best return, streak.

25
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:40,291
PERPDUEL.

26
00:01:40,241 --> 00:01:45,432
Real perp orders on testnet paper, a named opponent, and proof you can
open.

27
00:01:45,432 --> 00:01:48,225
Long or short: beat a person.

